# R36S V5 (Rockchip RK3326, aarch64): fragment on top of the kernel's arm64 defconfig,
# applied with scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh (design D7 of r36s-single-card).
# The build fails if any option here does not keep the requested value in the final .config.
#
# Already in the arm64 defconfig and not repeated: ARCH_ROCKCHIP, CPUFREQ_DT, I2C_RK3X,
# MFD_RK8XX_I2C, REGULATOR_RK808, COMMON_CLK_RK808, ROCKCHIP_DW_MIPI_DSI, PWM_ROCKCHIP,
# ROCKCHIP_IOMMU, ROCKCHIP_IODOMAIN, ROCKCHIP_PM_DOMAINS, IIO, KEYBOARD_GPIO, LEDS_CLASS,
# LEDS_GPIO, SERIAL_8250_DW, SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE, VFAT_FS, SQUASHFS, BLK_DEV_LOOP,
# BLK_DEV_INITRD, DEVTMPFS and DEVTMPFS_MOUNT.
#
# What the defconfig builds as a module and the console needs early is built in here, as
# on the GA36: the panel and fbcon (boot messages on the screen), the GPU, the PMIC
# (charger, codec), the gamepad and the filesystems of the boot. CPU frequency and thermal
# stay at the mainline defaults (OPPs and zones of rk3326.dtsi).

CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-r36os"
CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y
CONFIG_IKCONFIG_PROC=y

# Boot through the factory chain (D4/D5): the vendor U-Boot runs booti with our Image and
# DTB. The command line is this one (the boot.ini one does not count) and the initramfs is
# built into the kernel, as on the GA36. ttyS2 at 1500000 is the speed of the factory
# bootloader, so the serial never changes speed during the boot.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="root=PARTUUID=4c554d32-01 rootwait console=ttyS2,1500000 console=tty1 loglevel=6"
CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE="/initramfs/initramfs.cpio"

# Panel: VOP, DSI and its D-PHY, the ST7703 panel (variant in kernel/patches/0010), the
# PWM backlight and fbcon, built in so the verbose boot shows on the panel early
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP=y
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_VOP=y
CONFIG_PHY_ROCKCHIP_INNO_DSIDPHY=y
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SITRONIX_ST7703=y
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_PWM=y
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y
CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y

# GPU: Mali-G31 (Bifrost) with panfrost
CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST=y

# PMIC RK817: charger and fuel gauge (simple-battery in the DTS), RTC
CONFIG_CHARGER_RK817=y
CONFIG_RTC_DRV_RK808=y

# Audio: I2S1 and the RK817 codec in a simple-audio-card, with the speaker amplifier on
# gpio3 20 (simple-audio-amplifier)
CONFIG_SOUND=y
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC_ROCKCHIP_I2S=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC_RK817=y
CONFIG_SND_SIMPLE_CARD=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC_SIMPLE_AMPLIFIER=y

# Gamepad: buttons in gpio-keys and the two sticks in adc-joystick over the SARADC behind a
# GPIO multiplexer (io-channel-mux); r36os-padmerge joins them in user space (D8). joydev
# gives the js* device that the hardware summary looks for.
CONFIG_INPUT_JOYSTICK=y
CONFIG_JOYSTICK_ADC=y
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SARADC=y
CONFIG_IIO_MUX=y
CONFIG_MUX_GPIO=y
CONFIG_INPUT_JOYDEV=y
CONFIG_INPUT_UINPUT=y
# Bring-up only (task 4.6, boot 15): log every input event in the kernel log (kernel patch
# 0021), to see whether a press is lost in the kernel, in r36os-padmerge or in RetroArch.
# Remove after, together with the patch.
CONFIG_INPUT_EVLOG=y

# Temperature: tsadc (soc and gpu zones of rk3326.dtsi), so throttling works from the start
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_THERMAL=y

# Boot (D6): SD card, SYSTEM squashfs on loop, overlay with tmpfs, FAT BOOT and exFAT ROMS
CONFIG_MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP=y
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_ZSTD=y
CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y
CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=y
CONFIG_MSDOS_PARTITION=y

# Memory: compressed swap in RAM (ZRAM + LZ4)
CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
CONFIG_ZRAM=y
CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4=y
CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_LZ4=y
